{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KqXY4MeHv9PT4RysHt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written it as an email. I brought up the March error myself so David hears it from you, along with what you changed afterward. Under 400 words.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Request for promotion to Senior Paralegal\n\nDear David,\n\nI'd like to be considered for promotion to senior paralegal in the January review cycle. I've been a paralegal in the litigation group for five years. The senior role means supervising the other paralegals and making sure the group never misses a deadline, and I already do much of that work.\n\n**My work last year**\nI supported four lawyers on 23 cases, two of which went to trial. I billed 1,640 hours, 90 above the group's target of 1,550.\n\n**The deadline tracking sheet**\nIn 2023 I built the court-deadline tracking sheet our group uses. Two other groups in the firm now use it as well.\n\nI also want you to hear about a mistake I made in that sheet. Last March I entered a filing deadline wrong. Another paralegal caught it, and we filed two hours before the court's cutoff. That was too close. In April I added a second-person check, so a second person now confirms every deadline entered in the sheet. Since then we've entered about 600 deadlines, and none has been wrong or missed. I can't promise I'll never make another error. What I can promise is a system that catches errors before they matter, and I would hold the team to that standard as senior paralegal.\n\n**Training and supervision**\nI trained all three paralegals the group has hired in the last two years. As senior paralegal I would make that supervision formal. I commit to:\n\n- A short weekly check-in with the paralegals I supervise, to go over workload and upcoming deadlines and catch problems early.\n- Completing the state paralegal certification by June 2027.\n\nI understand the promotion comes with a $9,000 raise and responsibility for supervising the group's paralegals. I'm ready for both.\n\nCould we meet in person before the January review to talk about this? I'm happy to work around your schedule.\n\nThank you for considering my request.\n\nBest regards,\nJenna Morales\n</final_document>\n\nA few notes:\n\n- **The paralegal who left.** I wrote that you trained the three new hires but didn't mention that one left after 8 months. David probably knows. If he asks, it helps to know why they left, especially if the reason had nothing to do with their training.\n- **Whether the role is open.** The letter doesn't assume either way. Before you send it, it's worth quietly finding out whether the group has a senior paralegal slot. That's a good question for the meeting if you can't learn it sooner.\n- **Timing.** Send it well before December 15 so there's time to meet first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":10161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1075},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58b96930-210a-48a6-959b-60ea88676b5c","uuid":"8b521dfa-3f46-49ab-87b3-a91978f2f8de","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:35:14.407Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KqXJB8va57k38fgdC3"}
